    {
      "id": "bridge-contract",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "Contract",
      "position": {
        "x": 1320,
        "y": -350
      },
      "width": 720,
      "height": 380,
      "data": {
        "title": "Contract",
        "body": "**What data belongs to it?**\n\n```text\nbridge   { ref, resourceKind, scope, grants[], key?, exposure?, entryPort? }\n```\n\nOne record, `data.bridge`, and each fact once. `key` is the class key an import of a class grants; `exposure` is what an export offers; `entryPort` is the port an import enters by. Nothing else is stored: whether it is an import or an export is its type; the endpoint is the `ref` and the entry port; there is no second record, and no copy of its settings at the top of `data`. A loaded import carries those copies for the code that still reads them, and a saved one drops them. `components/GraphEditor/utils/bridgeRecord.js` does both, and `readBridgeSettings()` in `bridgeSettings.js` is the one place that reads a record for the editor. On an export, `exposure.events` lists the events it offers; on an import, it lists the events it shows as ports.\n\nRequired at minimum: the node type (`import` or `export`), `resourceKind`, `ref`. For `resourceKind: node-class`, also `key`.\n\nA node made from an imported class stores only its type (the class key) and `data.classRef`, the address of the class. It carries no copy of the class and no record of the import it came through; the app finds both when the graph loads. Grants are a different contract.",
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          },
          "baseLevel": "detail"
        },
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "bridge",
          "updatedAt": 1791592047776,
          "reason": "bridge-reference"
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "fe331a1c-0790-447b-ad05-83ddc1898214"
        },
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/templates/page-template/classes/page-section.node-class.node"
      },
